From edb75580780fcdfb05c64571339e19f438ecc17f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emdee52 <emdee7101@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 16:20:53 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] port(MB-4): split only the selected parts into their own
 objects

New action on a multi-part selection: "Split selected parts" moves exactly the
selected parts out, each into its own object at its current placement, and the
source object keeps every part that was not selected. 5 parts, 3 selected ->
4 items: the object with 2 parts plus 3 single-part objects. The existing
Split > To Objects (all parts, source removed) is untouched.

- libslic3r/OrcaExt/SplitParts: split_parts_to_objects() creates one object per
  selected MODEL_PART in the same model - the part's mesh, name, per-part
  settings and painting travel with it, and each new instance takes the
  composed transform (instance * part) so the part does not move. The selected
  volumes are then removed from the source with delete_volume(), which folds
  the last part's transform into the instances when one part is left.
- Refused (nothing changes) when the selection would leave the object without
  a model part, when a selected volume is not a model part, or when it is
  empty.
- GUI: the multi-selection menu's Modify submenu gained "Split selected parts"
  next to "Merge selected parts"; the gate shares its same-object / model-part
  / not-cut / not-text-SVG check with the merge action and additionally
  requires at least one model part to remain.
- MCP: new tool split_parts(object_id, part_ids) for the same path.
- Tests: four cases - the source and the untouched parts stay put, a rotated
  and translated part keeps its world placement, both copies of a part follow
  when the source has two instances, and the refusals.

libslic3r suite 1733/1733; runtime check over MCP on a 3-part cut object
(1 -> 3 objects, source keeps 1 part, extracted parts at their own z, slice
idle; the only new warning is the expected "too close to others", since the
extracted parts still share the source's footprint).
