Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 16:33:06 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] port(MB-4): allow splitting a single selected part, and offer
 it on the part menu

A single part row now works too: selected_parts_of_one_object() no longer
requires a multi-selection (it only needs one selected volume row), and the
part menu's Modify submenu carries "Split selected parts", since with one item
selected the context menu is the part menu, not the multi-selection one. The
merge action is unaffected (it still needs two parts to fuse).

Checked over MCP on a 3-part cut object: split_parts(0, [2]) -> 1 object
becomes 2, the source keeps 2 parts, the new object is the extracted one;
naming both remaining parts is still refused.
